Done. Acted on finding #2 only.

**Change** (`internal/cli/embed.go:77-79`): added a bounds check in `loadStaticEmbedder` right after the dim/vocab validation:

```go
if unkID < 0 || int(unkID) >= vocabSize {
    return nil, fmt.Errorf("embed model: unkID %d out of range [0,%d)", unkID, vocabSize)
}
```

This closes the one path where a corrupt asset crashed instead of degrading — an out-of-range `unkID` would have panicked later in `Embed` on the first unknown token (`e.matrix[base : base+e.dim]` out of bounds). Now it fails the load like every other corruption case, so `defaultEmbedder()` returns `nil` and recall falls back to lexical.

**Test** (`embed_test.go`): added `encodeTestModel`, a minimal model-byte encoder (the format previously had no test scaffolding), and `TestLoadStaticEmbedderRejectsBadUnkID`, which asserts a valid `unkID` loads and an out-of-range one is rejected at load. I confirmed it's a real regression guard — without the new check the load would succeed and the test would fail.

`gofmt`, `go build ./...`, `go vet`, and the full test suite all pass.

